        "title": "Can humans regrow a whole limb?",
        "sentences": [
          "Why can your body repair a cut but not routinely regrow a missing arm?",
          "Healing and regeneration are related processes, but rebuilding a complex limb requires far more than closing a wound.",
          "A limb contains coordinated arrangements of bone, muscle, nerves, blood vessels, and connective tissue with precise spatial organization.",
          "Some animals regenerate complex structures, giving researchers ways to investigate the biological signals that guide that process.",
          "Humans have limited regenerative abilities, including the liver’s ability to restore tissue mass after some injuries.",
          "That does not mean scientists can currently make an adult human regrow an entire lost arm.",
          "Regenerative medicine is promising, but a result in one tissue or species should not be exaggerated into universal replacement.",
          "Which structure sounds hardest to reconnect: nerves or blood vessels?"
        ],
